---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import HomepagePreview from '../components/HomepagePreview.astro';
import StructuralPreview from '../components/StructuralPreview.astro';

const indexLinks = [
  { slug: 'glossary', label: 'Glossary' },
  { slug: 'reference', label: 'Reference' },
  { slug: 'network', label: 'Network' },
  { slug: 'episodes', label: 'Episodes' },
  { slug: 'terrain', label: 'Terrain' },
  { slug: 'language', label: 'Language' },
  { slug: 'methods', label: 'Methods' },
];
---

<Layout title="Home" description="A visual companion to Gravity's Rainbow (1973).">
  <Nav slot="nav" />

  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <h1 id="home-title" class="hero-title wordmark"><span>The</span><span>Zone</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-description">
        a visual companion to <em>Gravity's Rainbow</em> (1973)
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav id="contents" class="contents" aria-label="Site sections">
    <p class="contents-intro">Despite all its unintelligible digressions, its great many technical terms in languages other than English, its historical documentary and reflections... reading <i>Gravity's Rainbow</i> is still one of those once-in-a-lifetime experiences.<br><br>Coming to Pynchon's 1940s Europe at a stage when my own life involves looking at the cross-talk between countless neurones has made me appreciate greatly the raw chaotic power of Pynchon's prose. Its encyclopaedic reputation and the ability to keep its hundreds of characters in its grasp sure are impressive, but browsing through Reddit and Substack, I have a feeling that these tags frequently turn people away from this masterpiece, frequently persuade people that 'one should <i>prepare</i> for <i>Gravity's Rainbow</i>', whilst the best part of the reading experience may be to lose oneself in all the chaos, digression, and confusion.<br><br>That being said, external guidance did help me a great deal with reading this admittedly difficult novel. This site is my attempt to provide a visual reading companion to my second favourite book of all time. And I hope, just as I found great happiness in understanding the <i>Brennschluss</i> calculation after reading Niklas Riewald's <a href="https://niklasriewald.com/category/gravitys-rainbow/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">'The math behind <i>Gravity's Rainbow</i>'</a>, other readers can do the same as they scroll through <i>The Zone</i>.</p>
    <ul class="contents-list" role="list">
      {indexLinks.map((link) => (
        <li>
          <div class="contents-entry contents-pending" aria-disabled="true">
            <span class="contents-label">{link.label}</span>
            <HomepagePreview slug={link.slug} />
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <section class="episode-field" aria-label="Episode word counts">
    <div class="episode-field-inner">
      <div class="episode-plate">
        <StructuralPreview />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer slot="footer" />
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero-inner,
  .contents {
    --homepage-gutter: clamp(4rem, 22vw, 22rem);
    width: min(100%, var(--measure-site));
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .hero-inner {
    padding: var(--space-xl) var(--homepage-gutter) var(--space-lg);
  }

  .hero-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 6.25rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 0.9;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    margin-left: -0.12em;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .hero-description {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
    font-family: var(--font-subtitle);
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .hero-description em {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .contents {
    padding: var(--space-lg) var(--homepage-gutter) var(--space-2xl);
    scroll-margin-top: calc(var(--nav-height, 3.5rem) + var(--space-md));
  }

  .contents-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 8rem));
    width: fit-content;
    column-gap: var(--space-md);
    row-gap: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 3rem);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .contents-list > li {
    min-width: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .contents-entry {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .contents-pending {
    color: var(--color-text-dim);
    opacity: 0.46;
  }

  .contents-pending :global(.homepage-preview) {
    filter: grayscale(0.78);
    opacity: 0.78;
  }

  .contents-label {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
    text-align: left;
  }

  .contents-entry {
    transform-origin: left top;
  }

  .episode-field {
    padding: 0 var(--page-gutter) var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .episode-field-inner {
    width: min(100%, var(--measure-site));
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-xl) 0 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }

  .episode-plate {
    min-width: 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .hero-inner,
    .contents {
      --homepage-gutter: var(--page-gutter);
    }

    .contents-list {
      width: 100%;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem 1rem;
    }

    .hero-title {
      font-size: 4.5rem;
    }

    .contents-entry {
      padding: 0;
    }

    .contents-label {
      font-size: 1.125rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 30rem) {
    .hero-title {
      font-size: 4rem;
    }

    .contents-label {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 22rem) {
    .hero-title {
      font-size: 3.4rem;
    }
  }
</style>
